# Install both `file:` dependencies as real copies instead of symlinks.
#
# `@neo4j-labs/nams-ai-provider` (typescript/packages/vercel-ai-provider) has
# its own node_modules with its own copies of `ai`, `zod` and
# `@ai-sdk/provider-utils`. A symlinked install resolves the provider's
# compiled `dist/*.d.ts` against *those* copies, while this example resolves
# its own — so `ai`'s branded `Schema<T>` type exists twice and TypeScript
# rejects tool/agent configs built from both sides (e.g. `session.withHooks`
# spread into `new ToolLoopAgent({ tools })`). One resolved copy is what lets
# the four programs here type-check with no `as unknown as` casts.
#
# Trade-off: after editing the provider's or the SDK's source you must
# rebuild it (`npm --prefix ../../packages/vercel-ai-provider run build` or
# `npm --prefix ../.. run build`) and re-run `npm install` here.
#
# Lockfile caveat: because both packages install as copies, package-lock.json
# records them inline. Those entries MUST keep `"resolved": "file:..."` — an
# entry without it makes `npm ci` fall back to the *published* package of the
# same version, which silently type-checks against different source. If
# `npm ci` ever installs a surface the local `dist/` does not have, delete
# package-lock.json and node_modules and run `npm install`.
install-links=true
